A live record whose `q/2` hashes to a different head than `q/1`, the request
before it on the same lane, with no `prefix.changed` row naming the change.

This is the direction none of the other `prefix.changed` refusals check: they
all confirm an EXISTING row is true of the two heads it names. A live record
computed both digests to write them, so a head that moved with no row
attributing it is a writer bug, not a fact about the run -- exactly the silent
miss #79 exists to replace.
